; NextDAAD SP16 Task 7 fixture - the AY characterization ladder, the
; STOPM repro and the BEEP scale.
;
; Compiled by tests\build-tests.ps1 on every run; staged as the active
; GAME.DDB in sd\AUDLAD\ by tests\build-tests.ps1 -AudLad, which also
; stages the five synthetic ladder songs generated by
; tests\audio\mkladder.py as
; 001.AKY .. 005.AKY, the kit's own 9-channel tune as 006.AKY,
; and GAME.AKY as a BYTE-IDENTICAL copy of 006.AKY - see "THE
; REAL MATERIAL" below for why that identity matters. sd\AUDLAD\ is
; emptied and refilled on every -AudLad run and holds nothing but this
; ladder plus a NEXTDAAD.NEX copy of build\nextdaad.nex - copy the
; folder to the card and launch from inside it.
;
; Owner leg instructions are EAR CARDS #T7A / #T7B / #T7C / #T7D in the
; SP16 Task 7 report. Nothing in this fixture judges audio quality -
; the interpreter cannot hear. Every verb here exists to put ONE known
; stimulus on the AY and stop.
;
; THE LADDER (#T7A). Five synthetic songs with strictly nested CONTENT:
; rung N's channels 1..N carry the same per-channel note streams as
; rung M's channels 1..N (the encoded blocks differ only in their own
; self-referential loop addresses, which move as the pool grows). Only
; the number of sounding voices - and therefore of sounding PSGs -
; changes between rungs.
;   LAD1 -> 001.AKY  1 channel   (PSG 1 only)
;   LAD3 -> 002.AKY  3 channels  (PSG 1 full)
;   LAD6 -> 003.AKY  6 channels  (PSG 1 + PSG 2)
;   LAD9 -> 004.AKY  9 channels  (all three PSGs)
;   LADQ -> 005.AKY  9 channels at volume 5 instead of 11
; LADQ is the discriminator: if LAD9 is distorted and LADQ is clean,
; the artifact is summing level, not channel count or PSG mixing.
;
; THE REAL MATERIAL (#T7A rung R, #T7B).
;   LADR -> 006.AKY  the kit's own 9-channel tune ("The Last V8",
;                    authoring-kit\AUDIO\1.aks -> 7487 bytes)
; GAME.AKY is a byte-identical copy of 006.AKY, so boot autoplay
; and LADR play the same bytes. This is not a convenience: it is the
; EXACT configuration of the 2026-07-23 STOPM sighting. In the kit,
; RELEASE\GAME.AKY and RELEASE\001.AKY are byte-identical (both built
; from AUDIO\1.aks == AUDIO\STARTER.aks by lib\audio.bat), so the tune
; that autoplayed and the tune MUSIC restarted at that sighting were
; already the same bytes. The synthetic rungs carry sustained
; software-only tones and nothing else; the real tune carries noise,
; hardware envelopes and retrigs, which is why the STOPM leg is run on
; IT and not on LAD1.
;
; THE BEEP SCALE (#T7C). AUTHORED ORDER IS "BEEP duration tone" - DRC
; reads Param1 as the duration (scaling it by 0.6 for ZX/NEXT), reads
; Param2 as the tone, REWRITES ANY BEEP WHOSE TONE IS OUTSIDE 48..238
; INTO A PAUSE, and only then swaps the pair for every ZX target
; (tools\DAAD-READY\TOOLS\DRC\drb.php:891-915). The interpreter
; therefore receives arg1 = tone, arg2 = duration (Task 1 order), but
; the SOURCE must be written duration first or every BEEP here silently
; compiles to a PAUSE. Task 1 also raised the pitch ceiling to 238, so
; tones 224-238 sound here for the first time. BEEPS walks a C major
; scale and then the whole new top octave; ORDER plays two beeps whose
; arguments are asymmetric in BOTH dimensions and whose swapped reading
; is also fully audible, so a swap changes what is heard rather than
; silencing it (see ORDER's own comment).

; System flags used by name (DAAD BLANK template spellings)
#define fPlayer             38
#define fDarkF              28

/CTL
_
/VOC
NORTH  2  noun
SOUTH  3  noun
LOOK   4  verb
LAD1   60 verb
LAD3   61 verb
LAD6   62 verb
LAD9   63 verb
LADQ   64 verb
LADR   68 verb
STOPM  65 verb
BEEPS  66 verb
ORDER  67 verb
/STX
/0  "It's too dark to see anything."
/1  "I can also see:"
/2  "What now?"
/3  "What next?"
/4  "What should I do now?"
/5  "What should I do next?"
/6  "I didn't understand."
/7  "I can't go in that direction."
/8  "I can't do that."
/9  "I have with me:"
/10 "I am wearing:"
/11 " "
/12 "Are you sure?"
/13 "Another go?"
/14 " "
/15 "OK."
/16 "Press any key."
/17 " "
/18 " "
/19 " "
/20 " "
/21 " "
/22 " "
/23 "I'm not wearing one of those."
/24 "I can't. My hands are full."
/25 "I already have the _."
/26 "There isn't one of those here."
/27 "I can't carry any more things."
/28 "I don't have one of those."
/29 "I'm already wearing the _."
/30 "Y"
/31 "N"
/32 "More..."
/33 ">"
/34 " "
/35 " "
/36 "I now have the _."
/37 "I'm now wearing the _."
/38 "I've removed the _."
/39 "I've dropped the _."
/40 "I can't wear the _."
/41 "I can't remove the _."
/42 "I can't remove the _. My hands are full."
/43 "The _ weighs too much for me."
/44 "The _ is in the"
/45 "The _ isn't in the"
/46 ", "
/47 " and "
/48 ".#n"
/49 "I don't have the _."
/50 "I'm not wearing the _."
/51 "."
/52 "There isn't one of those in the"
/53 "Nothing."
/54 " "
/55 " "
/56 " "
/57 "I/O Error"
/58 " "
/59 "File name error."
/60 "Type in name of file."
/MTX
/0 "NEXTDAAD AY LADDER FIXTURE (SP16 TASK 7)#n"
/OTX
/0 "a brass lamp"
/LTX
/0 ""
/1 "The listening room."
/CON
/0
NORTH 1
/1
SOUTH 0
/OBJ
/0    1   1   _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   _ _
/PRO 0
> _ _   AT 0
        PROCESS 6
> _ _   WINDOW 1
        WINAT 0 0
        WINSIZE 25 127
        CLEAR fDarkF
> _ _   WINDOW 1
        DESC @fPlayer
> _ _   PROCESS 1
/PRO 1
> _ _   PARSE 0
        REDO
> _ _   PROCESS 5
        ISDONE
        REDO
> _ _   MOVE fPlayer
        CLS
        RESTART
> _ _   SYSMESS 8
        REDO
/PRO 5
; ---- the channel-count ladder (EAR CARD #T7A) ----
; Every rung is SFX n 7 = load NNN.AKY and loop it. A rung that finds
; no file is a documented silent no-op, so a staging miss reads as
; silence, not as a distortion result - the card says to check the
; "playing" line before scoring a rung.
> LAD1 _  MES "rung 1: 001.AKY - 1 channel (PSG 1 A)#n"
          SFX 1 7
          DONE
> LAD3 _  MES "rung 2: 002.AKY - 3 channels (PSG 1)#n"
          SFX 2 7
          DONE
> LAD6 _  MES "rung 3: 003.AKY - 6 channels (PSG 1 + 2)#n"
          SFX 3 7
          DONE
> LAD9 _  MES "rung 4: 004.AKY - 9 channels (PSG 1 + 2 + 3)#n"
          SFX 4 7
          DONE
> LADQ _  MES "rung 4b: 005.AKY - 9 channels, volume 5 not 11#n"
          SFX 5 7
          DONE
; ---- the REAL material (rung R) ----
; The kit's own 9-channel tune, with noise, hardware envelopes and
; retrigs the synthetic rungs deliberately do not use. This is the
; material the SP13 kit-boot distortion sighting was heard on, and the
; material the STOPM sighting was heard on.
> LADR _  MES "rung R: 006.AKY - the kit tune, 9 channels, real material#n"
          SFX 6 7
          DONE
; ---- STOPM (EAR CARD #T7B) ----
; GAME.AKY == 006.AKY byte for byte, so LADR after STOPM replays
; exactly what boot autoplayed - the original sighting's configuration.
> STOPM _ MES "music stopped#n"
          SFX 0 8
          DONE
; ---- the BEEP scale (EAR CARD #T7C) ----
; AUTHORED ORDER IS "BEEP duration tone" - see the header. Param1 is
; the duration in centiseconds BEFORE DRC's 0.6 ZX/NEXT scaling, so
; 50 reaches the interpreter as 30 cs (15 frames, about a third of a
; second). Param2 is the tone: the jdaad pitch number, even, and it
; MUST be 48..238 or DRC turns the whole condact into a PAUSE. Index
; into the 108-entry equal-temperament table is (tone-24)/2; 120 = C4.
> BEEPS _ MES "BEEP C major scale from C4#n"
          BEEP 50 120
          BEEP 50 124
          BEEP 50 128
          BEEP 50 130
          BEEP 50 134
          BEEP 50 138
          BEEP 50 142
          BEEP 50 144
          MES "BEEP new top octave, tones 224-238#n"
          BEEP 50 224
          BEEP 50 226
          BEEP 50 228
          BEEP 50 230
          BEEP 50 232
          BEEP 50 234
          BEEP 50 236
          BEEP 50 238
          MES "BEEP scale done#n"
          DONE
; Parameter-order probe. Both beeps are deliberately ASYMMETRIC in
; their two arguments, and - unlike the earlier version - BOTH readings
; of BOTH beeps are legal, sounding notes, so a swap is heard as a
; DIFFERENT tune and not as silence (silence would be indistinguishable
; from a dead BEEP path).
; Authored durations 250 and 200 scale to 150 and 120 cs, so the DDB
; carries tone 180 / dur 150 and tone 216 / dur 120.
;   as written : tone 180 (1478 Hz) for 1.5 s, then tone 216 (4263 Hz)
;                for 1.2 s - a RISING pair, both very high, ~2.7 s
;                in total
;   swapped    : tone 150 (623 Hz) for 1.8 s, then tone 120 (C4,
;                262 Hz) for 2.2 s - a FALLING pair, both mid-range,
;                ~4.0 s in total
; So the swap signature is "two lower notes, falling instead of rising,
; and half again as long overall". Both swapped tones are even and
; inside h_beep's 24..238 window, so neither is rejected
; (src\overlay1.asm h_beep). An earlier version used BEEP 100 100 for
; the first note; that is symmetric in its arguments and detected
; nothing.
> ORDER _ MES "BEEP order: rising pair, high, about 2.7 s total#n"
          BEEP 250 180
          BEEP 200 216
          MES "BEEP order done#n"
          DONE
/PRO 6
> _ _   WINDOW 1
        WINAT 0 0
        WINSIZE 25 127
        PAPER 0
        INK 7
        CLS
        MESSAGE 0
> _ _   MES "Boot autoplay is GAME.AKY = 006.AKY (the kit tune).#n#n"
        MES "LAD1 LAD3 LAD6 LAD9 LADQ  channel-count ladder#n"
        MES "LADR                      the real 9-channel kit tune#n"
        MES "STOPM                     stop the music#n"
        MES "BEEPS                     BEEP scale + new top octave#n"
        MES "ORDER                     BEEP parameter-order probe#n#n"
        MES "Cards #T7A #T7B #T7C #T7D in the Task 7 report.#n"
        GOTO 1
/END
